    "title": {
      "en": "Blizzard Wants to Get Rid of BiS in WoW: Forever",
      "es": "Blizzard quiere acabar con los objetos «BiS» en WoW: para siempre"
    },
    "summary": {
      "en": "Blizzard Wants to Get Rid of BiS in WoW: Forever...",
      "es": "Blizzard quiere acabar con los objetos «BiS» en «WoW»: para siempre..."
    },
    "contentHtml": "\n            <div id=\"news-post-6aff6d0d79a515.60890883\" data-insert-ads=\"article\" data-zaf-dynamic=\"article\" data-units-dynamic=\"article\" data-zaf-slot=\"true\">In the latest episode of the WoW: Forever Podcast, Senior Game Designer Aidan Moon says he wants to get rid of the idea of BiS in WoW: Forever.<br><br><div class=\"wh-center\" style=\"text-align: -webkit-center;\"><div class=\"wh-youtube exclude-units lazy-load-background\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; background: url(&quot;https://i.ytimg.com/vi/67dDe3QgJtM/sddefault.jpg&quot;); max-width: 640px;\"><a aria-label=\"Play\" class=\"wh-youtube-inner\" href=\"javascript:\" style=\"padding-top: 56.25%;\"><i class=\"fa fa-play-circle\"></i></a></div></div><br><br>BiS, or \"Best In Slot\" gear, has been something that's existed in World of Warcraft since its inception. Players have looked to theorycraft their overall \"best\" items for every slot, to achieve multiple stat goals such as Hit cap, Expertise Cap, Critical Strike Immunity, while also maximizing their damage, Health, or Mana. However, developer Aidan \"Zirene\" Moon says he wants to try to \"get rid of BiS\".<div class=\"quote-box exclude-units\" data-type=\"user\" data-has-source=\"true\" data-has-toggle=\"true\"><div class=\"quote-source\"><a href=\"https://www.wowhead.com/forever/user=Moon\">Moon</a><span class=\"quote-said-text\"> said: </span></div><div class=\"quote-header\"><a class=\"quote-toggle\" href=\"javascript:\" aria-label=\"Toggle quote visibility\"></a></div><div class=\"quote-body\" data-markup-content-target=\"1\"><i>\"I essentially want to get rid of \"BiS\". I think that \"BiS\" is not a good thing for a video game that's supposed to be about role-playing systems about it. That's why I've introduced the creature subtype system, the biome system, and in the raid, it's different... In the raid, if you go to the left wing, that's 'snowy'; if you go to the right wing, that's 'haunted', so different parts of the raid will have different biomes. So I think your BiS should be different for every single boss if you're actually making a theoretical BiS list. It should be based on the creature and the biome. Itemization is 'I don't want you to think about BiS'; I just want you to think about the fight in front of you and how you're going to fight it.\"</i></div></div>Zirene clarifies that this design is both for the players who enjoy that intense level of optimization and for the player who just wants to go in and maybe be able to use a niche item they collected earlier in the game on certain encounters. Immediately following that conversation, the developers would clarify that players would eventually get bigger bags and better ways of organizing/<wbr>searching for specific items, since these new flavor items for biomes and creature types will continue to be added.</div>\n            \n            <noscript>In the latest episode of the WoW: Forever Podcast, Senior Game Designer Aidan Moon says he wants to get rid of the idea of BiS in WoW: Forever.<br /><br />BiS, or &quot;Best In Slot&quot; gear, has been something that's existed in World of Warcraft since its inception. Players have looked to theorycraft their overall &quot;best&quot; items for every slot, to achieve multiple stat goals such as Hit cap, Expertise Cap, Critical Strike Immunity, while also maximizing their damage, Health, or Mana. However, developer Aidan &quot;Zirene&quot; Moon says he wants to try to &quot;get rid of BiS&quot;.<br /><br /><div class=\"quote-box\"><br /><i>&quot;I essentially want to get rid of &quot;BiS&quot;. I think that &quot;BiS&quot; is not a good thing for a video game that's supposed to be about role-playing systems about it. That's why I've introduced the creature subtype system, the biome system, and in the raid, it's different... In the raid, if you go to the left wing, that's 'snowy'; if you go to the right wing, that's 'haunted', so different parts of the raid will have different biomes. So I think your BiS should be different for every single boss if you're actually making a theoretical BiS list. It should be based on the creature and the biome. Itemization is 'I don't want you to think about BiS'; I just want you to think about the fight in front of you and how you're going to fight it.&quot;</i><br /></div><br /><br />Zirene clarifies that this design is both for the players who enjoy that intense level of optimization and for the player who just wants to go in and maybe be able to use a niche item they collected earlier in the game on certain encounters. Immediately following that conversation, the developers would clarify that players would eventually get bigger bags and better ways of organizing/searching for specific items, since these new flavor items for biomes and creature types will continue to be added.</noscript>            \n        ",
